              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Decreasing the COX2 enzyme that makes inflammatory prostaglandin D2s to initiate and perpetuate the inflammation. \n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Decreasing the COX2 enzyme that makes the inflammatory prostaglandin E2 that binds to neurons to increase the propagation of impulses that are ultimately perceived as pain.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Decreasing the COX2 enzyme that makes the inflammatory cytokines, which go to the hypothalamus and signal fever\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, very few of our analgesics work at the level of the brain. The NSAIDs work in the periphery, decreasing the COX2 exzymes.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>Decreasing the perception of pain at thel level of the brain.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                }
              ],
